---
description: >-
  The markdownAlwaysOn twin of label-syntax.mmd: the same kanban labels
  with the setting on, so every label is markdown. The plain **bold**
  _ital_ column, card and quoted card labels draw bold and italic, the bare
  backticks and the code span draw inline code; tags, \n and quoted
  markdown strings draw as in the default picture, which this one differs
  from.
config:
  markdownAlwaysOn: true
---
kanban
  c1[column **bold** _ital_]
    k1[card **bold** _ital_]
    q1["quoted card **bold** _ital_"]
  c2["`column **bold** _ital_`"]
    k2["`card **bold** _ital_`"]
  c3[`column **bold** _ital_`]
    k3[`card **bold** _ital_`]
  c4[column a `code` b]
    k4[card a `code` b]
    q4["quoted card a `code` b"]
  c5[column <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O]
    k5[card <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O]
    q5["quoted card <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O"]
  c6[column one\ntwo]
    k6[card one\ntwo]
    q6["quoted card one\ntwo"]
